  "title": "Native writing on four fresh spaces",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Proved by hand: an acting atom has dissonance in its region in every state (P1, from lemma 3 of OTHER-ATOMS-20261110-001A), and a write changes only atoms the learner's probe finds unmet (P2). Exact: an atom acts exactly when its own constraints cannot clear its region, on every class of six spaces. Computed, frozen: a learner that sees only its own dissonance, the floor and the address asked for (a bit per atom, each atom given by its region) wrote 80 of 80 addresses exactly on four fresh spaces and each held after a disturbance, with no inexact stop; with the probe replaced by an instant check, 65 of 80 writes were inexact.",
